   <description>
      <short>
         <en>Sign in to GLPI with an email address as well as with the login.</en>
      </short>
      <long>
         <en>Users can sign in with their email address instead of their login. Only addresses that belong to a single user are accepted. GLPI keeps handling the password check, the account rules and two-factor authentication. A built-in brute-force protection locks repeated failed sign-ins. Settings: default or directory-synchronized addresses only, allowed domains, included and excluded users, sign-in log, and a list of the shared addresses to clean up.</en>
      </long>
   </description>
